@startuml returning_user_flow
!theme plain

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #888888

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
  FontColor #1A237E
  FontSize 13
}

skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3E0
  BorderColor #E65100
}

actor "User\n(Browser)" as User #FFF3E0
participant "SAML Service\nProvider (SP)" as SP #E8F5E9
participant "SAML-OIDC Bridge" as Bridge #E3F2FD
database "PostgreSQL" as DB #F3E5F5

title **Returning User — Session Already Exists**

User -> SP: Access protected resource
activate SP #C8E6C9
SP --> User: Redirect with SAMLRequest
deactivate SP

User -> Bridge: GET /saml/sso?SAMLRequest=...
activate Bridge #BBDEFB

Bridge -> Bridge: Check "saml_session" cookie - found

Bridge -> DB: Lookup session (not expired)
activate DB #E1BEE7
DB --> Bridge: Valid session found
deactivate DB

note right of Bridge
  Session still valid (within 10 min TTL).
  No OIDC round-trip needed.
end note

Bridge -> DB: Apply per-SP attribute mapping\n(if configured)
activate DB #E1BEE7
DB --> Bridge: Mapped session
deactivate DB

Bridge -> DB: Lookup SP metadata
activate DB #E1BEE7
DB --> Bridge: SP descriptor
deactivate DB

Bridge -> Bridge: Build & sign SAML Response

Bridge --> User: HTTP-POST SAMLResponse to ACS URL
deactivate Bridge

User -> SP: POST /saml/acs
activate SP #C8E6C9
SP --> User: Access granted
deactivate SP

@enduml
